Local changes by nemo, kept as commits on top of
upstream https://github.com/9fans/plan9port.
See git log upstream/master..master for the details.

acme
	Size (also in the row tag) makes all columns equal width;
	Newcol/Delcol resize, and the initial number of columns
	depends on the screen width.

	The wheel (and Magic Mouse) scrolls by the amount reported,
	not by a fixed step (see devdraw below).

	A window with + in the last element of its name is a scratch
	window; *.out windows get Get in the tag.

	! is a file name character.

	Getall (from Sape Mullender) does Get in all windows with
	a file, except scratch windows and those with an open
	event file.

	$acmetags has lines "regexp text": a window whose name
	matches regexp gets text in its tag instead of Look.

	Autoindent adds a tab after a line ending in {.

	$acmedump is the default file for Dump and Load.

	The "sys: child" note is ignored: it made acme kill its
	processes, dump, and quit when a child (e.g., the fontsrv
	used to load a font) exited early.

devdraw (macOS)
	Wheel events carry the scroll amount: bit 8 or 16 gives
	the direction, and the delta, shifted left one bit and with
	8 and 16 cleared, is or'ed in (acme uses buttons/4).
	A release follows each wheel event.

	New and resized windows are at least 64x64, so tiny windows
	(e.g., a one-line 9menu) no longer leave an empty image.

libdraw
	Programs using event(3) exit with status "hangup", not
	success, when the window is closed.

lib9
	getwd and cleanname show /Users/nemo/u as /u.

rcmain
	ifs is just newline by default; $home/lib/profile is read
	only if $_prof is unset.

9menu (new)
	Choose an item from a menu in a window and print its number
	(or its text with -t). With -i, a form: each item is a
	prompt for a text field (prompt=text gives the initial text),
	and Return prints the fields, one per line, with _ for an
	empty one. An item "label !cmd" runs cmd with rc when chosen;
	in a form, clicking its prompt runs cmd and puts its first
	line of output in the field. See 9menu(1).

9font (new)
	Choose a font from a list (fontsrv fonts, or font files),
	each name shown in its own font after a second without input
	(-d ms), and print its file name. Typing filters the list;
	Tab switches to typing the size. See 9font(1).

mac/Acme.app (new)
	Double-click to choose which acme to start, each with its
	own font, namespace, dump, plumber, and fontsrv, from
	profiles in $home/lib/acmeapp (rc files; samples in
	Resources/profiles). The menu can also create (New) and
	remove (Remove) acmes. Written in rc, using 9menu and 9font.
	When acme exits, everything serving in its namespace is
	killed. Logs to /tmp/acmeapp.$user.log.

Style
	Comments added in acme, devdraw, and the new programs use
	//, keeping /* */ for commenting out code.

Branches
	local-2023 is a snapshot of the sources installed at /u/plan9
	from 2023 to 2026; old-master-2021 is the previous master.
